From c71bfa047e9d7926eeef774b90ca72da14d3b088 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude (Lead Software Engineer)" <claude@sabush.local>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 07:12:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] UI Readability Amendment: WCAG-AA contrast/size fixes
 (styling-only, 23 items)

Corrects 23 governance-authorized instances where field labels, table
headers, and status text on financial, stock-count, closing/reconciliation,
navigation/business-identity, and superadmin operational surfaces rendered
below WCAG AA contrast (4.5:1) or below the app's own 10px caption floor.

Every replacement value is a token already documented in DESIGN_SYSTEM.md
or already in active use elsewhere in the same file:
  - text-gray-400 (~2.5:1) -> text-gray-500 (~4.8:1) on financial/stock
    labels and headers (Dashboard, Stocks, Add/Initial/Periodic Stock
    Count, Product Detail, Closing, Header, ShopSwitcher, Settings,
    report charts)
  - raw gold #D4AF37 (~2.1:1) -> documented darkened gold #8A6D1F
    (~4.9:1) on white (Header business-name eyebrow, ShopSwitcher,
    Dashboard unset-state Initial Capital card)
  - navy-at-60%-opacity (~2.1:1) -> gray-500, for consistency with
    sibling labels in the same modal (StocksView "remaining" figures)
  - 9px captions -> 10px, matching the app's existing floor (Closing
    summary, Product batch pricing, Dashboard product sub-labels)
  - dark KPI card supporting text opacity /35 and /40 (~3.1-3.7:1) ->
    /60 and /65 (~6.6-7.6:1) (Dashboard, ReportHome)
  - superadmin #64748b (~3.6:1) -> #94a3b8 (~7.0:1), already used
    elsewhere in the same files (BusinessDirectory, AuditTrail,
    BusinessDetail lines 108/165/177 only)

Styling-only: no workflow, business-logic, state, props, hooks, handler,
routing, or data-flow change. No new colors, classes, components, or
design-system tokens introduced. BusinessDetail.tsx:264 explicitly
excluded (already correct) per the Rule 8 discrepancy resolution.

15 files changed, 70 insertions(+), 70 deletions(-).

Governance chain: Audit -> Proposed Amendment (Sections A-C) -> Approved
-> Rule 8 Assessment (Resolved) -> Implementation Authorization (signed,
SABUSHIMIKE Masceni, Product Architect, 2026-08-19) -> Implemented ->
Verified -> Closed. See docs/engineering/ui-readability-amendment*.md.

Verification: typecheck clean (tenant/superadmin/server), production
build clean (both apps), 654/654 runnable tests pass across 36 test
files. 5 files requiring a live Firestore emulator were not executed
(storage.googleapis.com not in this environment's egress allowlist,
confirmed via a live download attempt) and are not reported as passed;
none of those files, firestore.rules, or server/ was modified by this
change. Contrast recomputed against final source values (all >=4.5:1).
Visual QA at 1280px/390px against the actual compiled CSS shows no
wrapping/clipping from the 9px->10px changes.

Docs: docs/engineering/ui-readability-amendment.md,
      docs/engineering/ui-readability-amendment-rule8-assessment.md,
      docs/engineering/ui-readability-amendment-implementation-authorization.md,
      docs/engineering/ui-readability-amendment-closeout.md
